## Iridium 1.0.20 - Per-User IP Limits

### Added
- **Per-user IP limit**: Each user can now have their own IP limit
- New `max_ips` field in user creation and editing forms
- Per-user limit stored in MongoDB, checked by IP Limit service
- If no per-user limit set, global limit is used as fallback

### Changed
- Updated `limit.sh` to check per-user `max_ips` from database
- Updated `add_user.py` and `edit_user.py` to support `max_ips` parameter
- Updated API schemas and endpoints for `max_ips` support
- Updated UI forms to include IP limit field (visible when IP Limit service is running)

### Technical
- `max_ips: null` or not set = use global MAX_IPS
- `max_ips: 0` in edit = reset to global limit
- `max_ips: N` = user-specific limit of N concurrent IPs
